    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the air starter motor, its inlet nozzle, the cranking shroud and the start valve clamp at the accessory gearbox pad, with the delivered and the revised clutch standards.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "To identify the air starter motor, its inlet nozzle and clamp, the cranking shroud and the start valve hardware at the accessory gearbox pad.",
      "figure_note": "The figure is drawn looking inboard with the fan cowl open. Item 20 and item 20A are the cranking shroud at the revised and the delivered standards; the revised shroud carries the larger inspection aperture through which the clutch witness mark is read and is the only way to tell the two apart when installed. The inlet nozzle at item 10 changes with the starter standard because the flow area differs, and the two must be ordered together. The pad seal is a consumable and is not listed as an item."
    },
